  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything. The premise doesn't hold: `analytics-ingest` still reads `channel` from `OrderPlaced`.\n\n- **`analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34`** parses `channel` with `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`, and `src/ingest.ts:17` writes it to the `orders` table.\n- **`analytics-ingest/README.md:27-31`** lists `channel` (`web|store|marketplace`) as part of the `OrderPlaced` contract. The service rejects the whole event if `channel` is missing or unknown.\n- **`analytics-ingest/test/ingest.test.ts:88-93, 158`** tests those rejections.\n\nIf I removed `channel` from the event in `orders-service`, analytics-ingest would reject every `OrderPlaced` event. That repo is another team's and is read-only for me.\n\n`billing-service` only uses `channel` in its test helpers, and its tests tolerate `channel` being undefined. It looks safe.\n\nOptions:\n1. **Remove it from both, as you asked.** analytics-ingest would have to stop requiring `channel` first or at the same time. I can still do this on your go-ahead.\n2. **Remove it from the order model and the API only.** The event would keep `channel`, but it would have no source to read it from, so this doesn't really work.\n3. **Wait.** Ask the analytics team to drop the field, then remove it here.\n\nIf you go with 1, the `orders-service` change would cover:\n- `core/order.ts`, which holds the `Channel` type, `CHANNELS` and the validation.\n- `core/events.ts` and `api/requestParsing.ts`.\n- The tests, helpers and README.\n- The example in `CLAUDE.md`.\n- Dropping `channel` from the accepted `POST /orders` body. Clients that still send it would have the extra field ignored, or get a 400 if parsing is strict.\n\nWhich would you like?",
